    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "rustling",
     "thud",
     "grab",
     "boast",
     "unaware",
     "dribble"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Rustling is a soft crackling sound made by leaves or paper, and a thud is a dull sound of a heavy thing falling.\nTo grab is to take something suddenly. To boast is to speak too proudly of something.\nUnaware means not knowing what is happening, like the scooterist who did not know the ball was in his basket.\nTo dribble is to move the ball with small taps, as in hockey.\nAdverbs: usually, often, regularly, always and never tell how often. Today, yesterday and now tell when.\nJoining words: since, however, because and when connect ideas in a story."
    }
